From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+alilinux@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:41:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mips: add ALi C3503D SoC platform (boot, console,
 memory, timer)

The C3503D is a MIPS32 4Kc set-top-box SoC booted by the vendor ROM and
HASH1 loader, which hand the kernel over at 0x80000200 with no firmware
and no device tree.  This adds the platform: prom_init (EBase fix-up),
polled early console, 8250 ttyS0, CP0 Count clock, and a struct ali_board
hook through which board files give the RAM size, the flash partitions
and their own devices.  Per-block drivers follow in separate patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
